311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (For systems where analytical solutions do not exist \(e.g., with nonlinear potentials or multi-particle systems\), machine learning models provide a way to generalize and predict results. By training on data generated from known physical systems, machine learning models can learn the underlying physics relationships \(e.g., the dependence of energy levels on mass and spring constant for 1D harmonic oscillator\).)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
