316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (This project aims to explore the use of machine learning techniques, such as Physics-Informed Neural Networks \(PINNs\), Random Forest \(RF\), and XGBoost \(XGB\), to efficiently predict quantum properties, including energy levels and wavefunctions, for one-dimensional systems \(specifically 1D harmonic oscillators\). The ultimate goal is to provide a faster, scalable, and more versatile alternative to traditional numerical solvers while maintaining high accuracy and physics consistency.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
